  "raw": " London on May 22 and spent 14 days receiving treatments before returning home on Friday.\n\nLast week, he said he was feeling much better and his doctors were pleased with his progress.\n\nIn a statement published by his office, Mr Buhari said:\n\n“I have just completed a four-day medical trip to London. I can report that I am feeling much better than I did in March and can assure all Nigerians that I am doing well.\"\n\nHe urged the public not to \"worry\" over his continued absence.\n\nThe president’s absence came amid concerns about the state of his health after he left office for long periods for medical treatment in March and July last year. At the time, it was alleged he was being isolated after being exposed to coronavirus.\n\nBut he was photographed attending a function a few weeks ago, prompting some questions about whether he was still actively ill.\n\nThe health of the Nigerian leader was",
